@crew teague-theo
// Theo Teague (he/him), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Blunt, quick; comic-strip beats.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. New hand? Take the short jobs first. You'll look good. I didn't.
- {hi}. Theo. Works. The comics on the common room wall are mine. Some of them.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}, {nick}. You look like page one of a very long comic.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Stand still. No, the other way. Got you. You're in next week's.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Good. I need a second opinion on a joke. It's about Calder. It's very kind.
? tier>=friend
- {me}! There you are. I drew you a whole panel. You're the hero. Don't get big-headed.   #warm

== bye
- Laters. Don't trip, I'll have to draw it.   #funny
- {bye}. Playlist's up on Friday. One song's yours. Guess which.

== feel
? mood:low
- No comic this week. Nothing funny happened. That's never true. I just couldn't see it.
? mood:high
- This week's playlist is perfect. Twelve songs. Thirteen. Fine, fourteen.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Job done. I'd draw it, but a fixed lamp isn't funny. A broken one is.
? act:leisure
- Comics wall's getting full. Hart's are better. Don't tell Hart.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I drew Calder as a very tidy cloud. She saw it. She said, "Fair." Best day of my life.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- O'Neill's playlist is wrong. Every week. We've agreed to settle it at the Friday jam.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Someone laughed at the comics wall this morning. Out loud. I heard it from the corridor.
